  "id": "kun_borrk",
  "name": "Kun-borrk (western Arnhem Land public song-dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Public song-dance genre of western Arnhem Land, sung in Kunwinjku and neighbouring languages around Gunbalanya (Oenpelli), in which a songman keeping time on clapsticks is joined by a didjeridu player to accompany dancing at funerals, ceremonies and festivals, each songman holding his own song sets. Kun-borrk was recorded at Oenpelli by the 1948 American-Australian Scientific Expedition to Arnhem Land and is the subject of continuing community recording projects.",
